WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.441
Model Context Protocol, often shortened to MCP, is a protocol pattern for connecting AI applications to external tools, data, resources, and services.

2
00:00:10.441 --> 00:00:20.072
The core idea is simple: an AI system is more useful when it can work with relevant context and approved capabilities outside the model itself.

3
00:00:20.072 --> 00:00:32.213
Instead of every AI application inventing a different integration style, MCP gives hosts, clients, and servers a more consistent way to describe and use external capabilities.

4
00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:37.473
A model is the component that generates or reasons over text and other inputs.

5
00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:42.815
An AI application is the product or environment that wraps the model for users.

6
00:00:42.815 --> 00:00:49.857
An agent is an application pattern where the system may plan, select tools, and take steps toward a task.

7
00:00:49.857 --> 00:00:53.984
An integration connects the application to another system.

8
00:00:53.984 --> 00:01:05.720
An MCP connection is one structured way to expose those integrations so the AI application can discover resources, call tools, or use prompt templates under defined rules.

9
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:16.404
MCP is often compared to a standard integration layer for AI applications because it separates the AI experience from the mechanics of each external system.

10
00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:28.949
A developer tool, a documentation source, a ticketing platform, a file system, a database, or an internal API can be exposed through a server with capabilities the host can understand.

11
00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:34.048
That does not mean every capability is automatically safe or appropriate.

12
00:01:34.048 --> 00:01:39.309
It means the integration surface can be made more consistent and governable.

13
00:01:39.309 --> 00:01:44.488
Developers care about MCP because it can reduce repeated integration work.

14
00:01:44.488 --> 00:01:51.692
Security teams care because it makes data flow, permissions, and tool use easier to inventory and review.

15
00:01:51.692 --> 00:01:59.300
Operations teams care because connected tools need ownership, logging, reliability, and incident response.

16
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:06.341
Product teams care because MCP can make AI features more useful without hard-coding every connection.

17
00:02:06.341 --> 00:02:12.735
The most important habit is to understand MCP as architecture, not merely as a plugin feature.
